Why See an Eye Specialist Instead of Treating Eye Problems on Your Own?

Blurred vision, redness, watering, eye pain, flashes, or floaters can have many different causes. While some problems may be minor, others can require prompt medical attention.

For example, glaucoma can damage the optic nerve permanently if it is not detected and managed appropriately. Similarly, sudden flashes, numerous new floaters, or a curtain-like shadow over the vision may indicate a retinal problem requiring urgent evaluation.

An ophthalmologist can:

Perform a comprehensive eye examination
Check vision and refractive errors
Examine the cornea, lens, retina, and optic nerve
Diagnose eye diseases at different stages
Monitor chronic conditions such as glaucoma and diabetic retinopathy
Recommend medicines, laser procedures, or surgery when appropriate
Provide long-term follow-up for ongoing eye conditions
